ction polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Ohio remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, and with the incumbent term-limited, neither party has a named nominee or candidate-specific polling to rely on. The forecast therefore rests on the state's partisan lean of roughly five points to the right, with no incumbency effect on either side.\n\nHeadlines from 2026 hint at a more competitive Ohio than recent presidential cycles: prediction markets favor a Democrat in the governor's race, state Democrats describe rare optimism, and national coverage describes Republican drag on issues like data centers. Those signals justify only a modest adjustment, since gubernatorial results and primary chatter rarely translate directly to presidential margins. The race sits in Lean Republican territory with wide uncertainty, and polling of the eventual nominees would sharpen the picture considerably.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2797, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3055, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.299, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3175, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3176, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3303, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3186, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3187, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3183, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3186, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3337, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3099, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3222, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3194, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3374, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3291, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3322, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3164, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": 